KZ3 patch 2163 (RSX pass 150): multi-entry program identity cache in get_pso (rsx_pso_memo.h).
get_pso kept a one-slot fragment-program memo (g_ld_fpm) and a one-slot vertex-program memo (g_ld_vpm); alternating programs
missed both and re-ran the FP size scan, the FP structural hash, the VP FNV, the texture-unit and TXL masks, the VP flow scans (per
draw, in ld_pso_key_tail) and rsx_fp_collect_constants. Two direct-mapped tables (VP by start slot, FP by location+offset, 16 entries
each) now hold the program bytes and the values derived from them; a hit needs a memcmp of the entry's bytes against the guest
bytes now (never reused unvalidated). The FP key hash is cached per (mode, VP seed), two results per entry. The VP size scan is
skipped on a hit (equal bytes end at the same end-bit instruction). Programs over the entry buffers (FP 8 KB) are never cached.
LD_PSO_MEMO_N=0 = the old single-slot code, 1..16 = entries per table (default 16), LD_PSO_MEMO_VERIFY=1 = recompute on every hit,
use the recomputed values, count mismatches ([pso-memo] lines). ld_xl_in gains vp_cached/vp_flow/vp_bbits so the key tail skips
its rsx_vp_has_flow / branch-bit scans. Host test tools/smoke/test_pso_memo.sh.

